    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe contiguous CP MoE output path all-reduces the full expert output and then selects each CP rank's local rows. When CP spans the entire TP group, reduce-scatter can directly produce the reduced local rows and reduce communication.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Use `reduce_scatter_tensor` in `MoeRowTransport.return_output` for the contiguous CP output path.\n- Enable it for CUDA tensors on non-HIP platforms when TP size, CP size, and TP group size match, and the row count is nonzero and divisible by CP size.\n- Allocate the local output buffer and retain the existing all-reduce/split fallback for other cases.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Manual four-GPU validation covered row ownership, empty and uneven inputs, noncontiguous inputs, fallback paths, and CUDA Graph replay. Exact-value checks passed for integer-valued inputs.\n- BF16 results can differ because the reduction order changes; bitwise equivalence is not guaranteed.\n- GSM8K: 1274/1319 correct with this change versus 1275–1279/1319 across unchanged baseline runs. Model-level accuracy parity is not yet established.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nProfiled DeepSeek V4.1 prefill on four H200 GPUs with TP=CP=EP=4, approximately 0.9\\0.7\\0.5 prefix-cache hit ratio.\n\nThe matched steps both use `[16240, 5120]` BF16 communication input and 40 MoE output collectives per rank. GPU kernel durations summed over those 40 calls:\n\n| Rank | All-reduce baseline (ms) | Reduce-scatter (ms) | Reduction |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 0 | 68.346 | 52.673 | 22.93% |\n| 1 | 71.672 | 57.369 | 19.96% |\n| 2 | 59.915 | 50.691 | 15.40% |\n| 3 | 60.526 | 44.981 | 25.68% |\n\nAcross six baseline and seven optimized nearby `bs=5` steps, mean MoE output communication time per rank decreased by 19.4%–21.7%. Mean forward GPU span, taking the slowest rank per step, changed from 606.244 ms to 595.320 ms in those samples.\n<img width=\"1512\" height=\"778\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a9cf0aef-e92f-4162-93a5-23cc0367feed\" />\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40852959562](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40852959562)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40852959432](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40852959432)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40852959560](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40852959560)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
